## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked

Explores a new DP angle: selecting exactly k non-overlapping substrings with a per-substring palindrome-anagram constraint, requiring fast feasibility testing via prefix masks and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Palindromable substrings via 26-bit parity mask
- Prefix XOR to test s[l..r] in O(1)
- DP over i and t with transitions from p-1
- Backpointer reconstruction; space optimization with rolling arrays
- Time complexity: O(n^2 k)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxLenPalAnagram(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] ^ (1 << (s.charCodeAt(i - 1) - 97));
  function popcount(x) { let c = 0; while (x) { x &= x - 1; c++; } return c; }
  function canPal(l, r) {
    return popcount(pref[r] ^ pref[l - 1]) <= 1;
  }
  // DP skeleton: dp[i][t] = max total length through i with t substrings
}
```

